  "Attributes": [
    {
      "Id": 759368,
      "attributeType": "LongString",
      "attributeName": "AIDescription",
      "attributeRelationType": "None",
      "Value": "## 12 Years Titron: A Commodore 64 Chronicle\n\n**Synopsis:**\n\nTwenty years after the chilling events of *1984*, Oceania remains under the iron grip of the Party. *12 Years Titron* plunges you into the life of Elias Thorne, a former Inner Party member who has defected and now lives in the shadows, haunted by his past. Titron, a revolutionary technology designed to monitor and control every citizen’s thoughts, has been perfected, tightening the Party’s control even further. Elias must navigate the treacherous underbelly of Oceania, evading telescreens and Thought Police while seeking a way to disrupt Titron and spark a flicker of rebellion.\n\n**Gameplay:**\n\nThis tense, atmospheric adventure combines exploration, puzzle-solving, and stealth elements. Utilize Elias’s knowledge of the Party’s systems to bypass security measures and uncover hidden pathways. Gather information, forge alliances with underground resistance groups, and manage your resources carefully.  The game features a unique \"Thought Meter\" – maintain composure and avoid suspicion, or risk attracting the attention of the ever-watchful Party.  Experience a haunting soundtrack and detailed Commodore 64 graphics that bring Orwell’s dystopian vision to life."
    },
